thread:
claire: quick follow-up from the batching review. we've seen repeated p99 blips when the batcher reorders across logical boundaries. two sketch ideas: (A) credit-based compaction limits per-tenant, and (B) explicit island fences so we never cross certain boundaries. want to converge on a prototype approach.

david: +1. credits sounded promising in the last meeting. how would credits be consumed? per-move or per-byte?

claire: per-move is simplest to start. small cost for a swap, larger for moving >X bytes. token-bucket per-tenant with control-plane resurfacing for pinned tenants. when credits hit zero we force strict enqueue.

mina: fences would solve ordering leaks for streaming sessions. can we combine both? fences for sessions + credits for general pooling.

claire: yes combine. fence_hint to pin requests to non-crossable islands (session:*, tenant:*, route:*) and credits to limit how much a tenant can be compacted into others.

david: telemetry needs: compaction_attempt, compaction_applied, credit_balance, island_id, moved_count, post_compaction_p99_delta. dashboards + correlated alerts.

mina: operational runbook idea: auto-stepdown AGGRESSIVE->GENTLE->NONE if post_compaction_p99_delta >5% sustained and credit_balance declining. add circuit-breaker to disable background coalescer if CPU overhead >3%.

claire: proto sketch (pseudo):

message Request {
  string route = 1;
  bytes payload = 2;
  enum CompactionHint { NONE=0; GENTLE=1; AGGRESSIVE=2; }
  CompactionHint compaction_hint = 3;
  string fence_hint = 4; // optional, e.g. "session:abcd"
}
queue.enqueue(Request r);

david: prefer explicit API queue.enqueue_compactable(req) to avoid proxies stripping fields, but proto field + header fallback X-Redwood-Compaction:v1 works for initial rollout. header must be fallback only.

mina: tests: mixed small+large workloads, kv-cache warmup regressions, stream starvation. I'll own dashboards, David can own stress tests.

ops-bot: preview branch "credit-handshake/islands-v1" created. smoke tests enqueued.

claire: acceptance criteria for canary: p99 delta <=5% over 7d, kv_miss_rate delta <=2%, compaction CPU overhead <3%. if fail -> automatic stepdown and alert to oncall. I'll draft the follow-up RFC and include the proto diff and rollout checklist. ping me to review. :rocket:
